Minkar: open the volume the loader was started from; RDRAND entropy

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
Copyright (c) 2026 The Minkar contributors
Part of Minkar.

The loader found its configuration, the kernel and its drivers with
LocateProtocol(SimpleFileSystem), which returns the first file system the
firmware knows. Under QEMU that is the boot disk; on a PC with several
disks it is often another disk's EFI partition, so the kernel was not
found and the loader returned to the firmware's boot menu without a word.
They now come from the loaded image's own device. When the kernel cannot
be loaded, the error stays on the screen for 15 seconds.

Firmware without EFI_RNG_PROTOCOL (QEMU has one through virtio-rng; many
PCs do not) left the kernel's random-seed uninitialized; the CPU's RDRAND
now fills it when the CPU has the instruction.

